// The `.` prefix typed in the REPL (plan §7f): `madc -i` loads this file,
// then the entries in testrepl_dotcmd.input run. cling's `.L FILE` is %load,
// `.type` reaches the table %type does, `.?` lists the commands with their
// aliases, `.5` stays C, and `.q` ends the REPL with status 0: the `exit(3)`
// typed after it never runs (it would fail the test's status).
int base = 7;
